#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""sharedbox-tools: system-wide toolchain for friends and their agents (root).

  sharedbox-tools install [--dry-run]    install everything enabled in sharedbox.conf
  sharedbox-tools update                 update the coding agents (+ uv); system packages are left to
                                         unattended-upgrades (Debian/Ubuntu) or the owner's pacman -Syu (Arch)
  sharedbox-tools force NAME [VERSION]   security: move everyone pinned below VERSION (default: the newest)
                                         of agent NAME (e.g. claude-code) onto the newest version now
  sharedbox-tools add pkg|npm NAME...    install extra packages and remember them (e.g. for `box request`s)
  sharedbox-tools remove pkg|npm NAME... uninstall packages (also remove them from TOOLS_* in sharedbox.conf)
                                         `pkg` = the system package manager (apt or pacman); `apt` still works
  sharedbox-tools status                 installed versions (also written to /var/lib/sharedbox/tools.json)

Only installs packages. It never upgrades the whole system, restarts services, or touches the network config.

Coding agents (TOOLS_NPM) are kept per version in /opt/sharedbox/agents/<pkg>/<version>, installed with pnpm
(one hard-linked store, ~40% less disk than npm; npm is the fallback if pnpm can't be installed), and /usr/local/bin
has a small shim per command. The shim runs the newest version, or the version the user is pinned to if
they chose `box updates manual`. A new version is installed next to the old one and switched to atomically,
so running sessions don't break mid-update. Pins are moved to the newest version when the pinned one has a
security advisory (npm audit) at or above AGENT_FORCE_SEVERITY that the newest one doesn't, or by `force`.
"""

